WHY THIS IS A SEPARATE FILE, AND WHY IT MUST STAY ONE
-----------------------------------------------------
DVRef places its public reflector data under CC BY 4.0. Its Acceptable Use
Policy (https://dvref.com/aup/) says "Public reflector data published by DVRef
is available under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
license", and its "Accessing DVRef Data" announcement of 2026-08-04 explicitly
permits mirroring, reformatting, commercial use, and the creation of "host
files, APIs, directories, and other services".

CC BY 4.0 section 2(a)(5)(B) forbids a redistributor from offering or imposing
"any additional or different terms or conditions on ... the Licensed Material
if doing so restricts exercise of the Licensed Rights". The rest of hamcall-db
is CC BY-NC 4.0 — non-commercial. Merging the DVRef rows into those artifacts
would impose a non-commercial restriction that CC BY 4.0 grants away, so it
would be a LICENSE VIOLATION, not merely untidy bookkeeping.

This is the same segregation discipline the project applies to the
OpenStreetMap-derived park grids (see LICENSE-ODbL), pointing the other way:
there the upstream is MORE restrictive than the project, here it is LESS.

Do not co-locate or merge these files into the CC BY-NC artifacts.

