STATEMENT OF MODIFICATION (required by CC BY 4.0)
--------------------------------------------------
The upstream rows were reformatted into this project's common reflector schema:
field names and structure differ from upstream, records from the four sources
were combined into one set per network, entries lacking a resolvable address
were dropped, and XLX registrations not seen by the registry in over 30 days
were treated as inactive and omitted.

EMAIL ADDRESSES WERE REMOVED from the free-text fields (`name`, `sponsor`,
`description`) and replaced with the marker `[email removed]`. These files are a
bulk-downloadable machine-readable artifact, which turns a sysop's address in a
reflector blurb into a harvestable list; the marker is left in place so the
surrounding sentence still reads. Field VALUES are otherwise unmodified.

D-Star entries are drawn from the XLX registry and the Pi-Star host files, and
DEDUPLICATED BY ADDRESS: the Pi-Star DExtra host file lists every XLX reflector
under its XRF alias at the same address, and those aliases are dropped so one
machine is not published twice under two ids. Standalone XRF reflectors are
kept even where their number collides with an unrelated XLX reflector's. REF
and DCS names from the Pi-Star DPlus and DCS host files are attached as
`aliases` to the row at the same address; they never create rows.

Derived fields computed by this project, which are not upstream data:
`port` for D-Star (30001, the DExtra protocol constant, which the registry does
not publish), `callsign` for XLX rows (the XRF-form name an XLX reflector
answers to on the DExtra wire), the matching `aliases` entry carrying that
same XRF-form name, and the provenance fields `license` and `alias_source`.

DVRef's Acceptable Use Policy — https://dvref.com/aup/ — also governs ACCESS
to DVRef's own infrastructure, which is separate from the license on the data.
It is why this project pulls from DVRef's API with an identifying User-Agent
and a per-account token rather than scraping their site or re-downloading from
third-party mirrors. Nothing in this file grants you access to DVRef's API;
mint your own token at https://dvref.com/accounts/token/.

The simplest way to comply is to redistribute this file unmodified alongside
the data.
